PORT=8080
LOG_LEVEL=info
NODE_ENV=development
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/circls

# ── Email ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two senders, picked per email. See docs/EMAIL_SETUP.md for the runbook.
#
# Customer + partner email (bookings, refunds, listing reviews, questions,
# invitations): MSG91 Email, on the same account/auth key as SMS. Key, from and
# template must all be set; with none of the email ones, that mail runs in STUB
# mode (writes a notifications row + logs `email_stub`, never delivers).
#   MSG91_AUTH_KEY           — the account auth key (owner-only to create).
#   MSG91_EMAIL_FROM         — sender on the domain verified under MSG91 →
#                              Email → Domains.
#   MSG91_EMAIL_TEMPLATE_ID  — the SLUG (not the numeric id) of the generic
#                              template (subject `Circls: {{VAR1}}`, body
#                              `{{VAR2}}`), for emails with no design.
#                              Designed emails use their own templates:
#                              `pnpm --filter @circls/api email:msg91-templates`.
#   MSG91_EMAIL_DOMAIN       — only if the registered domain differs from the
#                              from address's domain.
#   MSG91_EMAIL_DESIGNS      — designed emails that use their own (approved)
#                              template: "all" or a list of keys.
#   MSG91_EMAIL_TEMPLATES    — only if a design's template has another slug:
#                              "booking.confirmed=my-slug,…".
# MSG91_AUTH_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# MSG91_EMAIL_FROM=Circls <no-reply@event.circls.app>
# MSG91_EMAIL_TEMPLATE_ID=circls_transactional
#
# SMS through MSG91 is separate and OFF by default, even with the auth key set:
# MSG91_SMS_ENABLED=true
#
# Admin-team email (review requests, new organisers, payout reminders, daily
# summary): Resend, rendered here as HTML.
#   RESEND_API_KEY    — server key from https://resend.com/api-keys (starts re_…)
#   RESEND_FROM       — verified sender, e.g. "Circls Ops <ops@circls.app>".
#   ADMIN_TEAM_EMAILS — comma-separated recipients. Unset ⇒ no admin mail.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# RESEND_FROM=Circls Ops <ops@circls.app>
# ADMIN_TEAM_EMAILS=founders@circls.app,ops@circls.app
#
# Where replies to any Circls email go. Unset ⇒ no Reply-To, and the designs
# drop their "just reply to this email" lines.
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=support@circls.app

# ── Object storage (Cloudflare R2) — venue media ─────────────────────────────
# All four R2_* creds must be set for real uploads. If any is missing, storage
# runs in STUB mode (in-memory, per-process; uploads are not persisted).
# Create at: Cloudflare dash → R2 → Manage R2 API Tokens → Object Read & Write,
# scoped to the bucket. R2_ACCOUNT_ID is the hex prefix of the S3 endpoint.
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL is the bucket's public r2.dev URL (or a custom domain) and
# is what venue-image URLs are built from. The bucket MUST be public.
# SECURITY: this is the PUBLIC venue-media bucket. Do NOT put KYC/private docs
# here — those get their own private bucket.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# R2_BUCKET=circls-media
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.r2.dev

# ── Listing previews ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the short-lived "preview as a customer" links partners and reviewers
# open for unapproved listings. Any long random string (>= 16 chars). REQUIRED
# in production (boot fails without it — every instance must verify what any
# instance minted). Unset in dev, a random per-process secret is used, so links
# stop working on restart.
# LISTING_PREVIEW_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
